/P 92 0 R
/E (Alfido Tech is a technology-driven organization that offers internship and training programs for students and fresh graduates, with a focus on strengthening practical, industry-relevant programming skills. Rather than limiting learning to theory, the company structures its internships around hands-on tasks and real-world style projects, allowing interns to apply concepts as they are learned. Its core service areas include Software Development, Java Development, Web Development, and structured Internship Training aimed at building strong technical foundations for early-career developers.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (The primary objective of the Library Management System is to develop a computerized system that simplifies and organizes the various activities performed in a library. Traditional library management involves maintaining records manually, which can be time-consuming and may result in errors or loss of information. The proposed system helps overcome these limitations by providing a digital platform for managing books, members, and transactions.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (Another important objective is to centralize library information in one system. Instead of maintaining separate registers for books, students, and transactions, all relevant information can be stored in a database. This makes it easier for the librarian to access, modify, and manage records whenever required.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (The system also focuses on efficient book management. Librarians can maintain details such as book name, author, category, ISBN, quantity, and availability. The system helps identify whether a particular book is available, issued, or returned, making the process of managing the library collection more organized.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (The system aims to simplify the book issuing and returning process. When a book is issued to a student or member, the transaction can be recorded in the system. Similarly, when the book is returned, its status can be updated. This reduces manual calculations and makes it easier to track borrowed books.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (The Library Management System also aims to improve data accuracy and reliability. Since information is stored and updated digitally, the chances of incorrect entries, duplicate records, and missing information can be reduced. Proper database management also helps maintain consistency in library records.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
